^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Describe Spw as a metaphysical language in full: construct codex, sigil-property alignment protocol, production/manufacturing ladder past the screen, and industry integration briefs with pilots."
 ~#taste: "bridge-don't-fork; falsifiable metaphysics; editions with provenance; the language stays writable live and legible in capture"
}

^["development"]{
 lane: #semantic_rail
 ladder: #convention_to_manufacture
 develops: [#construct_codex, #sigil_properties, #drift_arbitration, #production_ladder, #industry_projection]
 review_surfaces: [@plan, @matrix, @operator_alignment, @atlas]
}

^["concept_index"]{
 primary: [#construct_codex, #sigil_property_matrix, #drift_ledger, #alignment_protocol, #labeled_braces, #coverage_algebra, #operator_deck, #edition_provenance, #sigil_physics_show]
 constructs: [#operator_sigils, #delimiter_couples, #label_escape, #positional_grammar, #semantic_expression, #file_idioms, #threshold_sequence, #composition_families, #registers, #dispatch]
 physics_axes: [#juxtaposition_envelope, #fundamental_motions, #object_kit, #higher_dimensions, #skim_anchors, #verso_legibility, #transparency_stack, #sound_writing, #stabilization, #evolution_fabric]
 industries: [#learning_science, #publishing, #library_science, #culinary, #rpg, #music, #show_production, #agent_tooling]
 tensions: [#codex_vs_second_canon, #arbitration_vs_fiat, #metaphysics_vs_falsifiability, #manufacture_vs_scope_creep, #stage_vs_canon, #spectacle_vs_instrument]
}

^["drift_ledger_seeds"]{
 ~#note: "Each row becomes a claim chain in the sigil property matrix before any registry or copy change."
 drift[at]{_001}: "@ = ref (author correction) vs 'enters perspective' (operator-alignment gloss); glyph lineage favors address/handle; candidate synthesis is ref-as-entered-perspective."
 drift[pct]{_002}: "% = meta/normalize (registry) vs measurement/reduction (author reads ratio/partition in the glyph); measurement-contract.spw is evidence surface."
 drift[amp]{_003}: "& subject sits between . and ^; may reduce into . as subject-as-traversal — pointing and reaching-into as one gesture."
 drift[hash]{_004}: "# repetition as dimensional channel tuning (# d1 time, ## d2 attention, ### d3 relationship, ##### d5 meaning) is used but undocumented."
 drift[und]{_005}: "_ as label/escape (?_query = probe named query) with intrinsic-operator history; holds a name flat against the grammar's tendency to interpret."
 drift[brace]{_006}: "Labeled braces {_A }_A permit overlapping non-nesting scopes ({_A {_B }_A }_B valid); load-bearing for selection spans; described nowhere durable."
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-07 00:10] observe - Canon is distributed: lineage/physics in operator-semantics.spw, registry in operator-alignment.spw, grammar/address split in sigil-identifier-contract.spw, expression syntax in semantic-braces.spw, atlas at /topics/software/spw/. No single construct census exists.
 >>[2026-07-07 00:10] observe - Three operator lists disagree on membership: original set (~ # . ? ! * & @ ^ <> () [] {}), site registry (adds = $ %, drops delimiters), operator-pages family list (#> #: . ^ ~ ? @ * & = $ % ! >). No surface names which list governs which layer.
 >>[2026-07-07 00:12] decide - New semantic-rail plan rather than extending operator-semantics-refinement: this track owns description + alignment + manufacture + industry projection, and cites the sibling plans for lineage and atlas work.
 >>[2026-07-07 00:14] semantics - The strongest metaphysical claim: Spw operators are sigils in the working sense — compressed intent that accumulates charge through attention and discharges through action. charge-cycle.spw and brace-gesture charge already implement this physics; the codex should say so explicitly and falsifiably.
 >>[2026-07-07 00:16] taste - Bridge-don't-fork is the codex survival rule. The codex adds a uniform entry shape and drift notes; owner conventions keep their content. A second canon would be worse than no codex.
 >>[2026-07-07 00:18] decide - Arbitration order for drift: author correction > glyph-property evidence > original-set lineage > site registry gloss > runtime label. No operator-meaning change lands without author sign-off (sensation-review-gates posture extended to semantics).
 >>[2026-07-07 00:20] observe - Manufacturing has an existing on-ramp: product-lines.spw editions/collectibles, seed-card infrastructure, the Spwashi Lego card schema, and the image pipeline from production-demonstration-pass. The new rung is 'manufactured artifact' with .spw sidecar provenance.
 >>[2026-07-07 00:22] decide - Industry sequencing: learning science, RPG, and agent tooling are load-bearing (live surfaces exist); publishing, library science, culinary are near-term; music and show production are exploratory, gated on a collaborator.
 >>[2026-07-07 10:05] decide - Workstream E added: a show presenting the sigils that IS the research instrument for their physics. Audience comprehension, transcription, verso/skim/dictation trials are the measurements. Segment anatomy: present, perform, probe (pre-registered expectation), precipitate (evidence + edition).
 >>[2026-07-07 10:07] semantics - Prefix/postfix juxtaposition read as one gesture seen twice: prefix wind-up, name contact, postfix follow-through. In sound this is literal ADSR: prefix anacrusis, name sustain, postfix release tail. Same-sigil sandwiches (!commit!) and asymmetric sandwiches (?name. vs !name?) test non-commutativity.
 >>[2026-07-07 10:09] semantics - Nine-motion basis proposed (strike, wave, loop, cross, settle, thread, lift, split, hook); every sigil decomposes into <=3 motions. Best single finding: _ is a ground-level thread that literally holds the name flat against interpretation — the glyph's geometry IS the drift-und-005 semantics. Also: @ as loop-around-settle (address embracing referent) is glyph evidence for drift-at-001; % as settle/split/settle and % as a two-note musical interval are independent evidence lines for drift-pct-002.
 >>[2026-07-07 10:11] semantics - Glyphs as stabilized motion: combinations of fundamental motions that survive six pressures (speed, scale, verso, skim, capture, sound) crystallize into letterforms. This is precipitates-and-projections at the glyph scale — the language's crystallization model explains its own alphabet.
 >>[2026-07-07 10:13] observe - Transparent substrate is a semantic medium: vellum overlays make the labeled-brace coverage algebra physical (stacking = composition, weaving band edges = interleaving), and verso reading is a selection pressure — mirror-symmetric sigils (= * # ^) survive back-reading; mirrored ? is the irony mark, so verso can invert meaning, not just orientation.
 >>[2026-07-07 10:15] taste - Evolution-fabric axis is the philosophy capstone and the easiest to inflate. It stays plan-local until sigil-evolution-005 has an evidence pass; the drift ledger is the fossil record and arbitration is documented selection, never silent replacement.
 >>[2026-07-07 10:17] maintain - sigil-physics-research.spw written with five claim chains (skim-001, verso-002, sound-003, motion-004, evolution-005), all untested; PLAN.md gained Workstream E, show risks, segment validation probes, and renumbered commits; show-production industry brief upgraded exploratory -> near-term since the show is its pilot.
 >>[2026-07-07 11:02] semantics - fable_charm section minted: ten cross-surface observations, each with saw/wisdom/toward shape, each discharging toward one plan direction. Strongest cross-site reading: the domain register is an operator atlas at biographical scale (newyear.life = threshold held annually, brainstorm.monster = ~ potential in public, clit.video = ! immediacy layered) — four longitudinal selection environments already running for the evolution fabric.
 >>[2026-07-07 11:04] taste - A charm is not doctrine: it spends charge when read and recharges only through disagreement plus evidence. The discharge_rule routes charm mismatches back into this stream so the charm stays falsifiable like everything else in the plan.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[codex_shape]: "One dense construct-codex.spw or a codex/ directory — at what entry count does the split rule from spw-surface-normalization trigger?"
 ?[sigil_craft_register]: "Is the charged-compressed-intent correspondence public copy or editor-layer lore? Strongest claim, easiest to misread as decoration."
 ?[cascade]: "If @ arbitrates to ref, does ~ narrow to potential/thread exclusively — and which copy surfaces cascade?"
 ?[brace_convention]: "Does the labeled-brace coverage algebra get its own convention now or after selection-span runtime stabilizes?"
 ?[second_artifact]: "After the operator deck, which industry earns the next physical artifact — recipe card or show cue sheet?"
 ?[deck_anatomy]: "Does the operator deck reuse the character-sheet card schema verbatim, or does a card-per-operator need a geometry panel the Lego schema lacks?"
 ?[episode_one]: "Single sigil (candidates: ~ or !) or one cross-sigil probe — the verso trial covers the whole set at once?"
 ?[show_medium]: "Live-first (staged episodes) or capture-first (TikTok-scale segments accumulating into episodes)?"
 ?[kit_order]: "Does the object kit precede the deck in manufacturing, since the show needs props before cards?"
 ?[signature_ownership]: "Who owns the sonic signature recordings as an edition — the musician, the show, or the language?"
 ?[sound_notation]: "Do sound signatures need their own notation, or does expression syntax suffice as a score?"
}

^["fable_charm"]{
 ~#minted_by: "Claude Fable 5"
 ~#minted: "2026-07-07"
 ~#register: "A charm is a small charged object left on the plan's mantlepiece. Each line was gathered by reading across the site's surfaces — conventions, philosophy, plans, product lines, the domain register — and each discharges toward one of this plan's directions. A charm is not doctrine; it spends its charge when read, and recharges only when someone disagrees with a line and brings evidence."

 charms: #[
  .{
   saw = `Every arbitrated drift in the ledger (@, %, &) happened where the gloss outran the glyph; every operator that never drifted (., !, ~) has geometry that does its own talking.`
   wisdom = `When gloss and glyph argue, side with the glyph — it has been paying rent longer than any registry entry.`
   toward = ~"./sigil-physics-research.spw#axis_composition_as_motion"
  },
  .{
   saw = `Across maintenance sweeps, the surfaces that survived (braces, charge, thresholds) all had bodies first — a route, an attribute, a gesture, a card — and canon followed. The ones that decayed were meanings without bodies.`
   wisdom = `Body before canon. Meaning that cannot be touched, clicked, stacked, or struck decays into ornament no matter how true it is.`
   toward = ~"./PLAN.md#workstream-c--production--manufacturing"
  },
  .{
   saw = `The drift ledger is the most trustworthy surface in this plan precisely because it records disagreement instead of smoothing it. The wip streams do the same at daily scale.`
   wisdom = `A language that publishes its own fossil record earns practitioners that a polished grammar never will. Keep the disagreements louder than the resolutions.`
   toward = ~"./sigil-physics-research.spw#axis_evolution_fabric"
  },
  .{
   saw = `? and ! pair everywhere on the site, but the wonder doctrine keeps ? senior — probes outnumber commits on every surface that feels alive.`
   wisdom = `On stage, open more questions than you close. Reading the open questions aloud is not humility theater; it is the show's immune system against its own charisma.`
   toward = ~"./sigil-physics-research.spw#show_format"
  },
  .{
   saw = `planning-ecology keeps every bridge thin, and the thin bridges are the ones still standing. That is ~ physics at plan scale: hold the path without collapsing it.`
   wisdom = `Keep the industry briefs potential-shaped. A brief that pretends to be canon gets archived; a brief that stays a held thread gets picked up.`
   toward = ~"./PLAN.md#workstream-d--industry-integration"
  },
  .{
   saw = `The domain register reads as an operator atlas at biographical scale: newyear.life is a threshold sequence lived annually, brainstorm.monster is ~ seed potential in public, clit.video is ! immediacy layered until it rewards.`
   wisdom = `Each site is one operator held long. That gives the evolution fabric four extra selection environments already running — the domains are longitudinal experiments that started before the research program had a name.`
   toward = ~"./sigil-physics-research.spw#axis_evolution_fabric"
  },
  .{
   saw = `The three audiences read three properties: engineers read grammar, illustrators read geometry and material, librarians read provenance — and those are exactly the columns every codex entry carries.`
   wisdom = `Simultaneous legibility and sigil alignment are one test wearing two costumes. If a codex entry serves all three readers, its sigil is probably well assigned; if one reader has no door, look for a drift.`
   toward = ~"./PLAN.md#workstream-a--construct-codex"
  },
  .{
   saw = `The best surfaces here charge on approach and discharge on return — prefix primes the skim, postfix pays the reread, and the wonder trail remembers the visit.`
   wisdom = `Design every page and every segment so the second pass is the gift. A language optimized only for first contact trains skimmers; one that rewards return trains practitioners.`
   toward = ~"./sigil-physics-research.spw#axis_skimmability"
  },
  .{
   saw = `The capture loop (screenshot to model to image and back) already selects glyphs and chrome for legibility, faster and more ruthlessly than any human reader.`
   wisdom = `Capture is fast-forwarded history: what survives the rig previews what survives transmission. Treat every capture pass as a free stabilization trial and log it as one.`
   toward = ~"./sigil-physics-research.spw#axis_stabilization"
  },
  .{
   saw = `Metaphysics inflates exactly where validation lags — the philosophy index knew this and demanded a counterexample per claim before this plan existed.`
   wisdom = `Five claims are untested. Keep them hungry: feed them probes, not adjectives. The day a claim gets confirmed by enthusiasm instead of a trial, retire the charm.`
   toward = ~"./PLAN.md#validation-loop"
  }
 ][reg=set]

 discharge_rule: `Point a collaborator at one charm before a working session and one direction after it. If a charm stops matching the surfaces — if a thin bridge collapses, if a bodiless meaning thrives — that mismatch is evidence, and belongs in the stream.`
}

